{"sourceSha256": "6faa569e4448531ed3ae31fd4c058347d33ceca801998dbd7e5a6fe674138356", "text": "5.constipation\n\nThe most common causes of constipation\ninclude a change in routine, not enough\nfibre in the daily diet, not enough fluids and\nlack of exercise.\n\nas fibre is indigestible, it adds bulk to the\nfaeces, making it more easily pushed along\nthe digestive tract.\n\none of the many benefits of regular exercise\nis improved bowel motility. Ideally, exercise\nshould be taken every day for about 30\nminutes.\n\nOver-the-counter laxatives are fine in the\nshort term, but seek advice if the problem\npersists\n\n6. Croup is an infection of the throat\n(larynx) and windpipe (trachea) that results\nin noisy breathing and a harsh, barking\ncough.\n\nChildren are small, so their airway is narrow.\nWhen infection causes swelling of the lining\nof the airway, it becomes even narrower\nmaking it difficult for the child to breathe.\nThis happens particularly when the air is\ncold, such as at night-time.", "pages": [{"number": 1, "text": "5.constipation\n\nThe most common causes of constipation\ninclude a change in routine, not enough\nfibre in the daily diet, not enough fluids and\nlack of exercise.\n\nas fibre is indigestible, it adds bulk to the\nfaeces, making it more easily pushed along\nthe digestive tract.\n\none of the many benefits of regular exercise\nis improved bowel motility. Ideally, exercise\nshould be taken every day for about 30\nminutes.\n\nOver-the-counter laxatives are fine in the\nshort term, but seek advice if the problem\npersists\n\n6. Croup is an infection of the throat\n(larynx) and windpipe (trachea) that results\nin noisy breathing and a harsh, barking\ncough.\n\nChildren are small, so their airway is narrow.\nWhen infection causes swelling of the lining\nof the airway, it becomes even narrower\nmaking it difficult for the child to breathe.\nThis happens particularly when the air is\ncold, such as at night-time.", "extraction": "ocr", "layout": 